{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "latlon3d_advection_vertical_zero_grad",
    "description": "MMS driver: forced vertical advection on the 3-D latlon3d grid, u_t = -w * D(u, lev) + w g'(z), discretized by grids/latlon3d/rules/central_D_lev_zero_grad_bc (2nd-order centered nonuniform interior, 2nd-order one-sided zero-gradient top/bottom, rank-3) on a SMOOTHLY STRETCHED vertical mesh -- the vertical (lev) analogue of problems/advection_1d_nonuniform_zero_grad with PASSIVE lon (NLON=8) and lat (NLAT=5) axes. Forced-steady manufactured solution u(z) = g(z) = cos(pi z), constant in time: u_t = -w g'(z) + w g'(z) = 0, so the discrete drift is pure operator truncation, second-order in L2 on the stretched mesh (supraconvergence, LeVeque 2007 sec 2.13). cos(pi z) has zero vertical gradient at z=0 and z=1, matching the one-sided zero-gradient top/bottom closures. VERTICAL MESH (grids/latlon3d edge-array contract): the consumer supplies ONE edge array pe (shape [lev_nodes], NLEV+1 values) for the quadratic stretch z(s)=0.6 s+0.4 s^2 on uniform computational nodes s_k=(k-1)/NLEV, i.e. pe[kn]=0.6((kn-1)/NLEV)+0.4((kn-1)/NLEV)^2 (pe[1]=0, pe[NLEV+1]=1), and the GRID derives the level centers zc via lev_center -- a first derivative needs only centers, not thicknesses. HYGIENE: pe aggregates over the node index kn (not k) so the inlined zc[k] does not capture the operator's k. A loader-API rebinding of NLEV re-sizes lev_nodes and re-derives the mesh. The forcing src=w g'(z) reads zc at runtime; the ic and references spell the stretched center zc[k]=(pe(k-1)+pe(k))/2 inline from literals and the NLEV name (build-time scope caveat), algebraically identical to the grid-derived zc, so the t=0 assertion is exact.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:latlon3d",
      "equation:advection",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.13 (nonuniform grids) and the supraconvergence discussion."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "VerticalAdvection3d": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/central_D_lev_zero_grad_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 8,
            "NLAT": 5
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Advected tracer over lon x lat x lev (horizontally uniform here)."
        },
        "w": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Constant vertical transport speed in the lev coordinate. Multiplies both the discretized derivative and the forcing so the steady balance holds for any value."
        },
        "pe": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Level-edge coordinates of the quadratic-stretch vertical mesh, pe[kn]=0.6((kn-1)/NLEV)+0.4((kn-1)/NLEV)^2 over node kn=1..NLEV+1 (pe[1]=0, pe[NLEV+1]=1, monotone increasing): the grid's single vertical geometry input over the NLEV+1-member lev_nodes axis. NLEV substituted at load (esm-spec 9.7.6) so a sweep re-derives the mesh. HYGIENE: the aggregation index is `kn` (node index), NOT `k`, so that when the derived zc = lev_center(pe) is inlined by variable index zc[k] into the vertical operator's aggregate over k, this pe body's index does not capture the operator's k (the non-hygienic-observed-inlining footgun propagates through the whole Design-B chain: grid lev_center uses gk, and the consumer's leaf pe must likewise avoid k/i/j)."
        },
        "zc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Level centers, GRID-DERIVED from pe by applying grids/latlon3d lev_center (zc[gk]=(pe[gk]+pe[gk+1])/2, hygienic index gk). Read by the vertical rule body for the center-to-center stencil spacings and by the forcing observed src."
        },
        "src": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "MMS forcing S = w g'(z) = -w pi sin(pi z) making u=cos(pi z) an exact steady solution of u_t=-w D(u,lev)+S. Runtime observed reading the grid-derived level centers zc[k] (free-name geometry resolves at evaluation); broadcast over lon x lat. Aggregation indices i,j,k."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i",
              "j",
              "k"
            ],
            "args": [],
