      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_vertical_transport_nonuniform_zero_grad",
          "description": "Forced-steady u(z)=cos(pi z) with w=1 on the quadratic-stretch vertical (b=0.4), independent of lon and lat. Source S=w g'(z)=-w pi sin(pi z) holds u steady. cos(pi z) has zero top/bottom gradient (zero-gradient closure compatible). References use the inline stretched centers zc[k]=(pe(k-1)+pe(k))/2 (build-time folds literals and NLEV only), identical to the runtime grid-derived zc. t=0 pins ic wiring; t=0.1 bounds the L2 error, which falls at the supraconvergent order 2. Per-resolution errors in the convergence golden.",
